                            <comment id="17022723" author="zstan" created="Fri, 24 Jan 2020 06:41:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;No visa found, i rerun TC. Test ok for me, just 2 comments from my side.&lt;br/&gt;
1. &lt;b&gt;1024&lt;/b&gt; - number in ticket description can mislead someone who not know default partitions count.&lt;br/&gt;
2. I still assume that additional ticket need to be filled for near dynamic threshold calculation fro IgniteOOME avoidance, what you think ? May be &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=irakov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;irakov&quot;&gt;irakov&lt;/a&gt; help somehow here ?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17022729" author="alex_pl" created="Fri, 24 Jan 2020 07:02:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I didn&apos;t request a bot visa since only one test was fixed and I&apos;ve run 3 test suites containing this test. Link to TC run attached.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Added info to the ticket description.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;I think we can&apos;t calculate it dynamically, it&apos;s hard task and I&apos;m not sure it worth the effort.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="17022837" author="zstan" created="Fri, 24 Jan 2020 10:25:59 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Seems besides Cache 2 suite timeout all other looks good, i rerun it, after green visa plz proceed.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
